From: Flavio Fisicaro <flavio@fisicaro.xyz>
Date: 2026-05-25
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: fix INIT_CREATE_STATIC to advertise the remote-heap page

`fastrpc_init_create_static_process()` allocates a remote-heap buffer
and sends a single-page descriptor (the heap's phys/size) in args[2] to
the DSP, but tells the DSP `inbuf.pageslen = 0`.  The DSP-side parser
reads `inbuf.pageslen` to know how many pages to consume from args[2];
seeing zero, it ignores the heap descriptor and the listener-PD setup
never completes, causing the FastRPC call to fail with -EPIPE.

The downstream Qualcomm driver (drivers/char/adsprpc.c) gets this
right: it sets `inbuf.pageslen = 1` whenever it allocates a fresh
remote-heap mapping, and `0` only on subsequent invocations (when the
heap is already known to the DSP).

Match that behaviour.  Track whether we just allocated the remote heap
in this call; if so, advertise pageslen=1 so the DSP picks up the
single-page descriptor it has been sent.

Symptom on Xiaomi Pad 5 (sm8150 nabu) with hexagonrpcd + an
`INIT_CREATE_STATIC` request for the SLPI `sensorspd` PD:

  hexagonrpcd[N]: Could not attach to FastRPC node: Broken pipe
  hexagonrpcd[N]: Starting /usr/bin/hexagonrpcd (INIT_CREATE_STATIC)
                  on /dev/fastrpc-sdsp

After this patch, the SLPI sensorspd PD creates successfully and the
Qualcomm Sensor Manager service appears stably on QRTR; the
~40-second-period SLPI crash loop (`remoteproc remoteproc0: crash
detected in slpi: type fatal error`) stops.

Fixes: 0871561055e6 ("misc: fastrpc: Add support for audiopd")
Signed-off-by: Flavio Fisicaro <flavio@fisicaro.xyz>
---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
index 1b735ee62..60bd5e435 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1572,6 +1572,15 @@ static int fastrpc_init_create_static_process(struct fastrpc_user *fl,
 		if (err)
 			goto err_name;
 
+		/*
+		 * Advertise the heap-page descriptor we put in args[2] on
+		 * this first init call (we just allocated cctx->remote_heap).
+		 * On subsequent calls the DSP already has the mapping.
+		 * Setting this only inside the vmcount/SCM branch below
+		 * loses it on channels with no heap VMIDs.
+		 */
+		inbuf.pageslen = 1;
+
 		/* Map if we have any heap VMIDs associated with this ADSP Static Process. */
 		if (fl->cctx->vmcount) {
 			u64 src_perms = BIT(QCOM_SCM_VMID_HLOS);
